Deploy a new MCPServer through the authenticated platform API identity. When .mcp metadata is present, deploy includes its image, tool side-effect metadata, prompts, resources, and tasks. If the server already exists, pass --update to redeploy it.

Usage:
  mcp-runtime server deploy [name] [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help                   help for deploy
      --image string           Container image repository (optional when .mcp metadata provides image)
      --metadata-dir string    Directory containing .mcp metadata files (default ".mcp")
      --metadata-file string   Path to .mcp metadata file
      --namespace string       Target namespace (optional when --team is provided)
      --port int32             Container port (default 8088)
      --replicas int32         Replica count (default 1)
      --scope string           Publish scope: tenant, org, or public
      --service-port int32     Service port (default 80)
      --tag string             Container image tag (default "latest")
      --team string            Team slug to resolve target namespace
      --update                 Update an existing server instead of failing when the name already exists

Global Flags:
      --debug      Enable debug mode with structured error logging
      --use-kube   Use direct Kubernetes mode with kubectl; requires admin/operator cluster access (admin/dev/test only)
